def case_note(r):
    notes={
      'eval001':'Expansion adds article 10 clause 3 and removes a non-gold initial chunk, but the missing low-risk definition remains outside final Top-5. The draft/final answer adds a low-risk mention and still abstains. Frozen groundedness falls from 1 to 0.5; the judge retains aggregate claim counts, not claim-specific reasons. No Answer Revision or Citation Revision occurred. Evidence removal of a required-point supporting chunk is not observed.',
      'eval002':'Answer Revision adds the ministry coordination/submission responsibility (P2) with citation E2. Draft text exactly matches the frozen Standard answer and the evidence content/citation map is identical. This is the strongest trace-consistent revision association; the frozen Standard audit is an exact-draft proxy, not a separately run draft audit.',
      'eval005a':'Expansion leaves ordered Top-5 unchanged. Neither answer covers any of the seven complete required propositions according to the frozen evaluator; the internal complete decision and success status disagree with benchmark completeness 0.',
      'eval005b':'Answer Revision and Citation Revision occur on unchanged evidence. The final answer adds transparency and incident-handling obligations (P4). Citation recheck passes, but the answer between the two revisions and the original validator errors were not retained. Their separate contributions cannot be isolated; the final completeness decision precedes Citation Revision.',
      'eval006':'Expansion leaves ordered Top-5 unchanged; all five quality metrics remain unchanged and Answer Completeness stays 1. The trigger sought another clause beyond the already satisfied frozen required points; this does not prove the trigger incorrect.',
      'eval010':'Answer Revision changes the reporting sentence, yet benchmark completeness stays 1. The final internal checker requests an explanation obligation associated with E5 beyond the two frozen required points and returns incomplete_answer. This illustrates a difference in target definitions, not a formal checker false positive/negative.',
      'eval013':'Expansion leaves ordered Top-5 unchanged. Answer Revision appends the highest-applicable-testing-level sentence, which was already in the frozen Standard answer. Citation Correctness and Groundedness fall to 0.8, while completeness stays 0.6. The final judge gives aggregate claim counts without locating its unsupported claim; no evidence establishes that revision introduced unsupported content.',
      'eval014':'Expansion leaves ordered Top-5 unchanged. The generated draft/final answer gives more detail for application forms and testing-project contents; the frozen evaluator gains P1, P2 and P4 despite continued abstention. Expansion did not introduce final evidence, so its contribution is not isolated from generation/evaluator variation.',
      'eval016':'Expansion leaves ordered Top-5 unchanged. The new answer omits several specific form identifiers present in Standard; the frozen evaluator reports higher citation correctness and groundedness, with unchanged required-point coverage. This is consistent with a narrower answer but does not isolate an expansion effect.',
      'eval022':'Answer Revision appends the agency database collection/quality/annotation responsibility with E1. The frozen evaluator gains P2 and improves all five oriented metrics, while P1 and P3 remain unsupported. Evidence stays unchanged; draft benchmark scores were not retained.',
      'eval026':'Answer Revision adds system description and intended use (E5), which the Standard answer already included. Final metrics remain at 1 for completeness/citations/groundedness and 0 unsupported rate. No gain over Standard does not exclude recovery from an incomplete Agentic draft.',
      'eval027':'No Substantive Intervention and unchanged initial/final evidence. Frozen evaluator loses P4 (innovation/social responsibility); the final internal checker still declares complete and success. Standard point labels are retained without per-point judge rationales, so generation wording and evaluator variability cannot be separated.',
      'eval029':'Answer Revision appends an impact-assessment report obligation (E4), while the two frozen required points and all five quality metrics remain unchanged. The added material extends beyond the frozen point set; it is not evidence of a wrong trigger.'}
    return notes.get(r['query_id'], 'No Substantive Intervention; Initial Retrieval, Evidence Coverage Check, Answer Generation, Answer Completeness Check and Deterministic Citation Check are recorded. '+('Internal complete/success disagrees with incomplete frozen benchmark coverage.' if r['agentic_answer_completeness']<1 else 'All frozen quality metrics are unchanged.'))

